            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Plus it's a great way to use up leftover grilled chicken or rotisserie chicken. I used 3/4 cup of Hellman's light mayo cut with 1/4 cup of reduced fat sour cream. I added a bit of curry powder for a little kick and I love the crunch from the celery. Since I didn't have any cashews on hand I added some chopped apple. This was perfect on toasted whole grain bread and didn't require any extra mayo or tomato, just some crisp lettuce - YUM!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "daldenmorse1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Make this the day before you need it. Sub green grapes for the cranberries or walnuts for the cashews as alternatives, and easy on the mayo, just enough is where you want it.",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-11T16:41:35.006Z"
          },
