              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sharonras"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this with leftover rotisserie chicken. It came out wonderful! I don't think I will use the tomato next time so the cranberry taste is more a highlight.",
            "datePublished": "2021-06-17T13:35:53.377Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MSPAX1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "5 stars tailored to my own preferences. Used a rotisserie chicken, grapes instead of cranberries and walnut pieces instead of cashews. Alot of my substitutes were based on what I had on hand or what was on sale. It was brought to my attention that the garlic powder addition was very well recieved...I never used it in this kind of dish until I saw in this recipe. I also added green onions which were on hand but I personally would have added some onion even though this was not in the recipe. Having said all that I will definately try this recipe as written.",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-31T18:42:04.617Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good with the modifications I made. I did 1/2 the mayo and 1/2 the cranberries based on user reviews, hence the 4 star rating on the original recipe. I also took out the celery and tomato due to personal preference, and because I had leftover Turkey used that instead of chicken. So good!",
            "datePublished": "2026-01-06T05:40:15.722Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sharon B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good! I used grilled chicken breasts. Only thing modified was , I had unsalted cashews.. Very nice balance of flavors. Next time, I make this, which I will; I am going to use croissants:-))",
            "datePublished": "2019-07-11T15:55:18.960Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mdatek"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Whole family loved it, even the picky eaters. No one wanted it as a sandwich. We ate it straight off the plate. Only change I would make is cutting back on the 1C mayo a hair. Makes it a touch soupy.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-02T20:03:12.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rainman2008"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this fairly often for lunches. My wife loves it and likes it even better when I add sliced red grapes to it. I use unsalted sliced roasted almonds instead of cashews and usually use the great canned chicken breast that I find at Costco unless I have leftover chicken.I cut back on the mayo by using some plain Nancy's yogurt. I eat it as a sandwich while my wife likes hers as a salad with some cottge cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-07T09:44:17.690Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Meghan Rodriguez Magner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't happen to have any leftover chicken, but was really in the mood for chicken salad, so I just used canned chicken. I also didn't have celery salt, so instead of using garlic powder, I just used garlic salt in place of both ingredients. I also added apple, as another reviewer suggested. And I used candied pecans instead of cashews. Serve it up on some toasted wheat bread...oh MAN it's good! It's like a Waldorf Chicken Salad Sand! Mmmm...",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-04T11:07:45.590Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "joelcaryn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy, delicious and so colorful! A big hit at our house. The only things I did differently were: I used pecan bits instead of cashews, seasoned with a pinch of salt and a dash of paprika at the end, and I added a little pineapple juice to moisten it. My husband thought it was great, but thinks I should add more dried cranberries next time. I've been wanting to make chicken salad for months and I'm so glad I chose this recipe. I'll definitely be making it again and again.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-13T06:40:19.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LivelyCow1858"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Two things take this up a notch from your average chicken salad - the fact that the chicken has previously been grilled and rested (for even more flavor), plus the crunch and sweetness from the cashews and cranberries. A big hit in my house for lunch!",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-19T13:26:53.698Z"
          },
